WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.160
Ah Skip, here we go again...

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:08.000
It’s time for us to take another crack at
putting SCP-682 six feet under, once and for

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:08.560
all.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.320
If you’ve been following this channel for
any amount of time, then there’s one thing

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:18.560
you know for certain: SCP-682 is harder to
kill than pretty much, well, anything!

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:23.120
We’ve made multiple videos on the Foundation’s
failed attempts to finally terminate the beast,

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.520
and we made a video with some of your ideas
on how to finally slay the monster.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.920
And considering you’re watching this video
right now, you can probably guess how that

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:32.640
went.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.440
Now it’s time for one more run at the Death
Star: and once again it’s with your ideas

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.240
from comments and community post responses,
let’s see if any of them can help us finally

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.800
put this ill-tempered reptile to rest.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.160
If we can’t…

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:50.480
well we’re not blaming you, but also it’s
your fault.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.680
Let the community termination attempts commence!

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.880
Anais McBride suggested, “Ask the Witch
Child.”

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.320
SCP-239, also known as The Witch Child, is
one of the most dangerous and powerful anomalies

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:02.960
out there.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.760
She’s a small girl with&nbsp;
unparalleled reality-warping&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.240
mental abilities, so powerful that her very

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.960
brainwaves alone can be passively fatal.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.520
However, the problem is,&nbsp;
her power is so potentially&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.680
dangerous that she’s forever kept in a kind

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.160
of medically-induced anomalous coma.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:23.200
Dr. Alto Clef thinks she’s so dangerous
he’s even campaigning to have her terminated.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:29.600
As a result, the O5 Council has forbidden
any cross-testing between 682 and 239, fearing

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:35.840
the consequences of 239 gaining 682’s powers
and becoming a truly unstoppable threat capable

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.280
of causing an XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.360
Syed Zamin Ali Shah Kazmi Mushadi suggested,
“Kill him with SCP-734.”

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.520
This is an interesting one.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:54.160
SCP-734, also known as The Baby, is an anomaly
that causes a painful degenerative disease

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:58.880
that eventually disintegrates the entire body
and kills the victim if they so much as come

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.680
into contact with the baby or its fluids.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.320
However, based on cross-tests with other,
similar “touch it and die” anomalies like

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:12.480
SCP-409 - the Contagious Crystal - we can
probably guess how exactly this would go down.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.040
In all likelihood, the Baby’s anomalous
effects would infect and destroy large portions

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.440
of SCP-682’s body.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:25.200
However, at this point, 682 would adapt to
the threat, and begin to reverse it and heal.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:30.720
Even worse, it’s likely that 682 would steal
the ability for a limited time, and become

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.160
deadly to the touch.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.960
Caden Griffin suggested, “Why don't you
use the Dragon Slayer to terminate 682?

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.320
It has proved itself many times in fights
with LSAs.”

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:46.240
SCP-5514, the Dragon Slayer, is essentially
a giant fighting robot designed to take down

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.960
killer kaijus with its&nbsp;
plethora of state-of-the-art&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.200
anomalous weapons and defenses.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.920
However, we’d still argue that while it
could definitely help in immobilizing 682

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.000
during a rampage, it doesn’t have much of
a chance of actually killing it.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.520
Let’s look at SCP-001, the Gate Guardian,
a supernatural warrior with a blade hotter

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.880
than the sun, capable of cleaving atoms in
half.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:12.320
Even he couldn’t kill SCP-682.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:16.720
So a robotic approximation with only a fraction
of the Gate Guardian’s power is probably

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:20.160
not going to have any real chance of killing
682.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:25.440
ImAChuckster48 suggested, “Make it bite
its tongue so hard that it just destroys itself.”

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.720
While we can certainly attest from personal
experience that this really, really hurts,

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:36.160
we worry that if ever 682 bit its own tongue
really hard, it’d just drive it into a state

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.760
of murderous rage.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.840
Though we do take a small piece of satisfaction
in knowing its tongue would probably be in

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.560
distress for a few minutes afterwards, it’s
unlikely to wipe out the beast once and for

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.120
all.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:53.360
Liezel Rolle suggested, “How about we just
put SCP-682 in 2317's cell.”

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:59.600
SCP-2317 is an old wooden door that functions
as a portal into the domain of a planet-destroying

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:04.960
monster known as The Devourer of Worlds, a
being that many believe is associated with

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:10.640
the Scarlet King, and will inevitably escape
and cause an XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:15.200
While you may be thinking, “Perhaps it’ll
kill 682”, it’s more likely that they’d

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.560
collaborate, seeing as they both want the
same thing.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:20.320
Namely, to kill everyone.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:25.040
If you let 682 in, chances are, it’ll come
back through that door with the Devourer right

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:28.640
on its tail - then, it’s all of our problems.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:33.520
Guest123 116 suggested, “Drop him in Russia
so they can terminate him.”

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:36.400
The Foundation has technically already tried
this.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:42.560
They dropped 682 into SCP-3930, a patch of
literal non-existence in Russia that causes

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.600
anything that goes inside of it to cease to
exist.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.720
And afterwards?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.840
He was fine!

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.520
So yeah, dropping him anywhere in Russia is
probably just going to get a bunch of innocent

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.360
Russian civilians killed.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.600
Mysher said, “The Foundation shouldn't worry
about how to kill him, but how to stop his

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:58.880
ability to adapt.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:05.200
I would suggest typing "Scp 682 no adaptability
juice" or something like that into SCP-294

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.760
and then kill him by any means, which SHOULD
kill him forever.”

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:16.160
An interesting theory, but what if he simply
adapts to SCP-682 no adaptability juice?

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.720
Then we’d really be in trouble...

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:23.280
MarioTGP said, “Give him a twitter account,
he'll be canceled instantly for his spicy

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:24.080
opinions.”

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:30.000
SCP-682 would cancel Twitter itself, for not
having opinions that are spicy enough.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.040
Sorry, Jack.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:37.040
SCP-096 - still sore about losing the battle,
we assume - said, “Let him fight the queen

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:37.760
of England.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.520
After all, she’s immortal too.”

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:44.400
We definitely think it would be interesting
to see SCP-682 go head to head with the Queen

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.120
of England.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:49.600
Based on all the knighting she does, we know
that she at least has a sword, though we don’t

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:53.200
know if that sword is as powerful as the one
wielded by the Gate Guardian.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:57.520
But regardless of the outcome, the battle
would definitely change history.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:03.120
Every history book would simply read: “SCP-682
Punched the Queen”, everything else would

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.400
just be a footnote.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:08.880
Noah Cordero said, “Use SCP-2935 to kill
the lizard.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.200
As you can see in the video, he will die.”

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:17.920
SCP-2935, also known as O’ Death, is probably
one of the scariest and deadliest SCPs out

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:18.400
there.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:24.080
It killed an entire alternate dimension, including
an alternate SCP-682.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:30.240
The problem is, putting our 682 into 2935’s
alternate reality could lead to the destruction

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.480
of our entire dimension.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.280
Why’s that?

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:39.440
Because, if 682 was somehow able to return
to our world from the world of 2935, it could

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:44.160
bring the spirit of death itself back with
it and kill us all in the process.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:49.760
Explorando con beto 1 suggested, “SCP 682
vs Lady Dimitrescu.”

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:55.440
While Resident Evil 8’s Lady Dimitrescu
has certainly captured all of our hearts,

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.880
we don’t think she’ll be bringing home
the W on this one.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:04.320
Lady Dimitrescu has a powerful adaptive ability
of her own - with a high resistance to damage,

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:09.920
impressive regenerative abilities, and a number
of offensive capabilities, from huge claws

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.760
to a powerful dragon form.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:15.600
However, considering she wasn’t even able
to defeat Ethan Winters, she probably wouldn’t

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:19.200
be able to defeat SCP-682, either.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:25.120
However, in her dragon form, SCP-682 may finally
join the rest of us in developing a crush.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:26.560
Or is that being crushed?

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:28.240
Anyway, moving on.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:34.160
Jonathan Pecany suggested, “Just ask SCP
343 on how to destroy it, or even better,

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:35.760
ask if he could destroy it.”

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:40.320
It’s an idea so good that the Foundation
actually tried it, and it went about as well

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:41.600
as you can expect.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:47.200
When the SCP known as God entered the containment
chamber, he couldn’t even see 682 in there,

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.160
as though the creature was somehow totally
invisible to him.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:55.360
When God eventually got bored and left, they
told him that he was in there to destroy 682.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.840
He simply replied, “He's not one of mine.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.360
Deal with him yourself.”

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:01.120
Interpret that how you will.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:06.480
12 Escobar Blancas Eddy Saul suggested, “They
could send him to Area 37 for The Sisters

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:07.920
to experiment with.”

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:14.640
SCP-1765, The Sisters, are a trio of terrifyingly
powerful reality warpers that have taken over

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:20.720
Area 37, and spend their days tormenting everyone
inside with their twisted experiments.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:26.160
Using them to try to terminate 682 leads to
similar problems with using the Witch Child

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:31.440
or the Devourer of Worlds: If they decide
to team up rather than fighting, or the Sisters

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.200
take over 682, we’d all be effectively doomed.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:40.480
Kiroyah suggested, “Would the ants from
SCP-743 tear 682 apart?”

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:46.240
The Foundation actually tried this, getting
682 to consume chocolate from the SCP-743

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:49.600
fountain, incurring the wrath of its flesh-eating
ants.

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:54.560
However, 682 developed an adaptation that
gave it a long, ant-eater-like tongue, that

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:58.320
it then used to consume the ants faster than
they could consume it.

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:03.520
And even worse, the chocolate seemed to enhance
its regenerative abilities even more for several

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.480
days afterwards.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:08.800
Lol 2222 suggested, “Write the name in the
Death Note.”

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.080
Great idea.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:15.200
We’ll put it into practice as soon as you
can tell us SCP-682’s real name.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:20.160
It may come as a surprise, but its parents
didn’t actually name it the “Hard to Destroy

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.120
Reptile.”

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.040
Stephen Vierie suggested, “I thought that
maybe we should put him in a giant blender

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:29.520
and then when he is in small pieces put lava
in the blender so it will incinerate him then

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:33.680
put nuclear waste into the blender and repeat
that until there is no more left of him.”

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:38.400
After the cooking whisks last time, we feel
obliged to include at least one attempt to

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:43.520
kill SCP-682 with oversized kitchen equipment
in every video about him.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:47.680
However, this attempt would probably go about
as well as the last one, we’re afraid.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:52.720
Extreme physical trauma by conventional means
- like burning and dismemberment - has never

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:54.560
been successful in the past.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:58.960
And the Foundation is extremely hesitant to
use anything radioactive on the beast, in

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:02.560
case it adapts and adds deadly radiation to
its own arsenal.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:06.480
MrMaster IQ suggested, “Just take away his
plot armor.”

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:12.960
You can pry SCP-682’s plot armor from its
cold, dead claws, and as we’ve already learned,

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:16.240
making those claws cold and dead seems next
to impossible.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.200
Moving on.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:22.480
JC3 suggested, “HMMM IF ANYBODY CAN'T BEAT
THE UNDYING LIZARD WHY NOT OMNI MAN I MEAN

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:27.040
HE DID KILLED ALL THE GUARDIANS OF THE GLOBE
OF COURSE HE CAN KILL SCP-682.”

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:33.440
Omni-Man from the comic and TV series Invincible
is undeniably a formidable opponent, given

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:37.680
he’s able to destroy superhero teams, cities,
and even planets.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.160
However, one of the few enemies to give Omni-Man&nbsp;

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.880
a genuine run for his money&nbsp;
is a genetically-enhanced

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:44.880
Kaiju known as Hail Mary.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:50.000
Given that, first, 682 has taken on beings
stronger than Omni-Man - like the Gate Guardian

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:55.120
- and lived, and second, that Omni-Man has
struggled with monsters before - chances are,

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:57.920
he probably couldn’t permanently kill this
one, either.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:03.680
Heycani Havea suggested, “Kill SCP-053,
then 682 will be sad and die.”

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:06.480
Wow, now that’s cold-blooded.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:10.720
However, even if this did work, it’s important
for you to remember that it’s impossible

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:15.760
to actually kill SCP-053, also known as The
Child or the Little Girl.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:18.160
Part of her anomalous abilities is that anyone&nbsp;

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:20.960
who attempts to kill her&nbsp;
will themselves immediately

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:24.560
die during the process - normally due to a
heart attack.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:29.920
So this method would result in a pile of dead
Foundation personnel, and no progress.

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:32.560
Jerry Zhang said, “Mush peanut butter on
it.”

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:37.440
This would definitely work if SCP-682 has
some kind of severe peanut allergy.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:40.720
After all, anaphylactic shock is no laughing
matter.

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:46.160
However, in the far more likely event that
this will have no effect on SCP-682, you will

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:49.440
likely just die with your hands covered in
peanut butter.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.680
Andrew Mills suggested, “My idea?

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:55.840
Have several Xenomorphs, Predators, and Daleks
(yes that’s a Doctor Who reference) take

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.280
682 on.”

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.560
Once again, in all likelihood, this would
have no effect.

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:06.480
682 has survived blades and lasers - the primary
weapons of the Predators and Daleks - and

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:11.440
spends the majority of its life immersed in
powerful acid, so the xenomorph would hold

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:12.960
no surprises for it.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:16.640
Sadly, this three-way teamup would be no match
for 682.

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:22.960
And even if they did defeat him, whoever wins,
we… well you know how it goes.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:26.320
Matteo Huang suggested, “Maybe just destroy
reality.”

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:27.040
This.

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:33.920
This might be the thing that finally kills
SCP-682, but considering it’s already survived

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:38.960
being thrown into pure nothingness in Russia,
it may just result in it being one of the

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:42.160
only survivors of a full destruction of reality.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:44.240
We, on the other hand, would all be killed.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:48.480
Though in a sense, we wouldn’t have to deal
with SCP-682 anymore.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.720
So maybe that’s a type of winning?

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:55.440
And finally, Blind Honor suggested, “Would
Saitama be a good way to eliminate it?

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:57.280
He is One Punch Man, after all.”

00:12:57.280 --> 00:13:01.600
Of anyone we’ve covered in this series,
Saitama from One Punch Man would probably

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:08.000
be the most likely to kill SCP-682, especially
if he was taking the battle seriously.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:12.400
After all, he has killed planet-destroying
monsters before with barely any effort.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:16.560
The only real question is whether he could
even be bothered to come down to a Foundation

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.720
containment site and fight it.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:22.000
Saitama hasn’t been known to be a very motivated
guy.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:27.200
But of course, like with anything, there’s
the risk that 682 would survive and gain his

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.080
powers.

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:29.760
Which would be bad.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:30.560
Awesome.

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:31.440
But bad.

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:34.880
Do you have new ideas for how SCP-682 could
be killed?

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:38.720
Do you thinkin you have the key to finally
bringing this beast to a well-deserved end?

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:43.200
Let us know down in the comments, and keep
an eye on our community posts for more SCP

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:46.960
questions like this one so you can be featured
in the next video!

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:53.600
Now go check out “Termination Attempts SCP-682”
and “How to Kill SCP-682 - Theories and

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:58.320
Ideas” for more futile attempts to murder
the Foundation’s orneriest reptile!

